# mtplx-131k-q8-stability-loop
owner: mtplx-131k-stabilizer · cadence: after every session-budget change · status: SUGGESTED
**I see q8/swap is the only known non-OOM 131K path — want a loop that confirms it stays stable for the 35-token/800-token and 5K/100-token jobs?**

## Prompt
Each tick: start MTPLX at 131K with `--paged-kv-quantization q8 --allow-swap` and current override env, run the 35/800 and 5K/100 prompt pair, record tok/s, OOM status, and memory usage, append to the 65K-vs-131K wiki page, fail open if OOM returns.

## Evidence
> **131K context now works with q8 KV cache!**
> Results with `--paged-kv-quantization q8 --allow-swap`: 35 tokens -> 800 tokens = 6.9 tok/s; 5K tokens -> 100 tokens = 0.6 tok/s; No OOM.
